  FILE = {Wei and Hung - The Impact of the Central Bank Communication Chann.pdf:/Users/corywhitney/Zotero/storage/J8H77WNF/Wei and Hung - The Impact of the Central Bank Communication Chann.pdf:application/pdf},
  KEYWORDS = {bin, read CW},
  ABSTRACT = {The central bank’s monetary policy formulation has increased demand for transparency in both developed and developing economies. The market generally believes that central bank communication can improve market efficiency and ease market volatility. This paper investigates the extent to which the central bank’s communications affect the foreign exchange rate of the New Taiwan Dollar (NTD) in the Taiwan financial market. Using the method of Wei, Lu, Chen and Hsu (2017), six central bank communication indicators are constructed and applied in our empirical analysis, with reference to Chang (2013), Kang et al. (2017), and Su et al. (2019). First, the empirical results show that the central bank’s speech is crucial and has a major impact on the currency market. Second, in terms of market expectations, KRW, RMB and JPY have a positive impact on the NTD, indicating that informal communication about international trade impacts the central bank’s communication. In general, the transparency of the central bank helps to reduce the information asymmetry of market participants and achieves more effective communication policies.},
